Subject: feat(write): merge a record's own sentences into one list entry

Card 26 (2026-09-25). run_grounding_pass grounds a multi-sentence
finding value as several sentences that all cite the same record
(item 11.34), and core/graph.py's listing builder walks those
sentences one row at a time with no dedup, so a three-sentence
abstract shows as three rows under one heading. Adds
merge_sentences_by_citation to synthesis/answer_layout.py: collapses
entries sharing a finding's citation_id into one, sentences joined in
survival order, first-occurrence position kept. The actual row-split
loops live in core/graph.py's listing and plain_listing closures,
outside this fence; the exact call sites are named in
testing/Developer/reports/2026-09-25_phase_8.4/builder_F.md for
whoever owns that file tonight.


